# NEGATIVE CONTROLS for integer exactness: two false identities whose coefficients pass 2^53, where a JavaScript
# number rounds. Both were PROVEN before 2026-10-02 (the mill read literals with Number(), and the provers combined
# coefficients in doubles). Expected: 2 refusals. Run: sh deck/term/deck/seed.tree/tmp/make-probe.sh
# test/case/number/exact-control.tree

# FALSE: 2^53 + 1 is not 2^53. A ring normalizer on doubles rounds the left coefficient onto the right one.
rule probe-coefficient-beyond-two-to-the-fifty-three
  mark x, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        read x
        code 9007199254740993
      call multiply
        read x
        code 9007199254740992

# FALSE, the same after a product: (2^27 + 1)^2 = 2^54 + 2^28 + 1, and 2^54 + 2^28 differs from it by 1.
rule probe-coefficient-from-a-product
  mark x, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        call multiply
          read x
          code 134217729
        code 134217729
      call multiply
        read x
        code 18014398777917440
